  "description": "An exploded plan of the generic hearing room: the wall clock and the exhibit cabinet (with the chart lying on its exhibit) rise out of their places; the display board, the specialist at the lectern and the participants stay. Only the supplied relationships are drawn, edge to edge, with their kind. A tracer follows the supplied traversal; once it reaches the board the chart settles on it with its reference (● measurement, as supplied), a band marks the supplied span, the explanation card comes out at the specialist's side and a connector draws from the span to it (◆ the specialist's interpretation, as supplied); both places get the same neutral frame. Fictional data; illustrative; the interpretation is neither right nor wrong, and no rule, weight or outcome is shown.",
